From 8ef798995cedf2ddefe3eb616a26856f82590411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CounterStrikeXB2 <cs2@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: console identity from the player's EEPROM; a router
 behind the NIC (CounterStrikeXB2 local patch)

console_id.c loads the player's eeprom.bin (checksums checked) for the factory EEPROM queries and the whole-EEPROM block reads XNet makes, the NIC's MAC, and XboxHDKey from RECOMP_XBOX_HDKEY or decrypted with the player's BIOS EEPROM key; nothing secret is logged. nvnet_nat.c is a router at 10.0.0.1: the NIC's DHCP hands out 10.x.y.z/8, Insignia's DNS first; UDP is relayed through host sockets (same port when free), IP fragments both ways, ARP and ping for the router; TCP is refused for now. Frames to other consoles still take the system link. RtlNtStatusToDosError maps facility-7 statuses to their low word (XOnline waits on ERROR_IO_PENDING). XboxKrnlVersion reports the retail 1.0.5838.1.
